Auto-detect header row in CSV/XLS imports, skip metadata rows above it

- Scans first 30 lines for a row with >= 2 known column header keywords
  (date, description, amount, balance, narrative, memo, etc.)
- For CSVs, reads raw lines to avoid parser errors from ragged metadata
- For XLS, uses pandas with header=None to scan
- Metadata rows above the header (bank name, account number, period, etc.)
  are automatically skipped
